  },
  "dt_log": {
    "__comment": "[TRACE FIXTURE -- the centre of the scenario] One row = one die transferred into a DT tape cell. | BUSINESS KEY IS (dt_job, dt_x, dt_y), NOT the spec draft's (dt_job, core_x, core_y). A single DT wafer mixes dies from SEVERAL core wafers (user 2026-08-01), so two different core wafers can each hold a die at core (5,5) and the draft key COLLIDES -- the second row would overwrite the first and the loss would be silent. (dt_job, dt_x, dt_y) is a physical destination cell and is unique by construction. Frame ambiguity does not threaten this: whichever of the 8 frames dt_x/dt_y are in, two dies still cannot occupy one cell. | dt_lot/dt_slot are the INFERENCE TARGETS -- 40% absent, and 10% PRESENT BUT WRONG, which is worse than absent because a wrong value makes a join succeed quietly. They are kept out of the key for that reason: a guess must never sit inside an identity. | dt_job is '<equipment>_<time>_<tapeslot>' and is certain. Tape slot != DT slot (the operator moves wafers by hand) but the tape->DT slot mapping PRESERVES MONOTONIC ORDER -- that constraint is what turns this inference from impossible into 'generate candidates, confirm once'. | core_lot/core_slot or core_wafer: at least one is always present. core_wafer, where present, is an ANCHOR.",
    "business_key": "dt_cell_key",
    "composite_key_source": ["dt_job", "dt_x", "dt_y"],
    "composite_key_separator": "_",
    "column_types": {
      "dt_cell_key": "string",
      "dt_job": "string",
      "dt_eqp": "string",
      "product": "string",
      "dt_lot": "string",
      "dt_slot": "string",
      "dt_x": "number",
      "dt_y": "number",
      "dt_index": "number",
      "core_lot": "string",
      "core_slot": "string",
      "core_wafer": "string",
      "core_x": "number",
      "core_y": "number",
      "c_bn": "string",
      "event_time": "string"
    },
    "display_columns": [
      "dt_cell_key",
      "dt_job",
      "dt_eqp",
      "dt_index",
      "product",
      "dt_lot",
      "dt_slot",
      "dt_x",
      "dt_y",
      "core_lot",
      "core_slot",
      "core_wafer",
      "core_x",
      "core_y",
      "c_bn",
      "event_time"
    ],
    "map_key_columns": ["dt_job"]
  },
