  "dt_map": {
    "__comment": "[DERIVED -- do not write by hand] Projection of dt_log produced by the DT map chain rules. A hand-written row here silently disagrees with the next replay. | MAP KEY IS (dt_lot, dt_slot) -- the PHYSICAL UNIT, not the acquisition unit. A map is one wafer, and one wafer can be fed by SEVERAL dt_jobs; that convergence is the point, because the same physical die written by two jobs must be ONE row or the layering invariant and the human-correction rule cannot apply to it. | dt_job is therefore NOT key material: it travels with the cell as its SOURCE. That is what makes a cell traceable and what lets the chain retract exactly one job's contribution (dt_map_derivation.plan_retraction) -- replace_map cannot, because a purge is scoped to a whole map and would delete a sibling job's cells to correct this one's. | A job with no confirmed (dt_lot, dt_slot) yet produces NO MAP: chain_key_gate refuses the unkeyed rows and names the blank column. That is rollout progress, not a defect. | Each cell carries its origin (core_wafer/core_lot/core_slot/core_x/core_y) because one DT wafer mixes dies from several core wafers, so the map's own key cannot recover where a die came from. That provenance is the difference between a map you can draw and a map you can trace.",
    "business_key": "cell_key",
    "composite_key_source": ["dt_lot", "dt_slot", "dt_x", "dt_y"],
    "composite_key_separator": "_",
    "column_types": {
      "cell_key": "string",
      "dt_lot": "string",
      "dt_slot": "string",
      "dt_job": "string",
      "dt_x": "number",
      "dt_y": "number",
      "dt_index": "number",
      "c_bn": "string"
    },
    "display_columns": [
      "cell_key",
      "dt_lot",
      "dt_slot",
      "dt_job",
      "dt_x",
      "dt_y",
      "dt_index",
      "c_bn"
    ],
    "map_key_columns": ["dt_lot", "dt_slot"]
  },
  "bonding_log": {
    "__comment": "[TRACE FIXTURE] Bonding record. b_bn is the bonding bin -- the DEFECT this whole fixture exists to trace back to a core die. | dt_lot/dt_slot here are the values AS OF BONDING TIME and they differ from the ones dt_log recorded at DT time, because split/merge moved the wafer in between. THIS IS WHY A SQL JOIN CANNOT SOLVE IT: joining bonding_log.dt_lot to dt_log.dt_lot does not error, it matches the WRONG wafer plausibly. The join has to be (key + as-of when) and then walk the lot_event chain. | bond_x/bond_y carry a third independent 8-way frame ambiguity -- the same primitive applies here as at core->dt, which is what 'universal' means (one primitive, N applications), NOT a third spelling of the same code.",
    "business_key": "bond_cell_key",
    "composite_key_source": ["bond_lot", "bond_slot", "bond_x", "bond_y"],
    "composite_key_separator": "_",
    "column_types": {
