  "dt_job_attribution": {
    "__comment": "[TRACE FIXTURE -- enrichment DERIVED table] One row per DT job; the worklist for inference #1 (confirm dt_lot/dt_slot). Rows are produced by the synthesized enrichment dedup chain from dt_log -- nothing ingests this table directly. | business_key is dt_job and decision_key is [dt_job], which satisfies the loader's contract (business_key IN decision_key). | THE TARGET COLUMNS ARE SUFFIXED '_confirmed' RATHER THAN REUSING dt_lot/dt_slot. A virtual join exposes them back onto dt_log, and a virtual column that COLLIDES with a real one merges absent-only -- so on the 10% of rows carrying a WRONG dt_lot the recorded wrong value would win and the confirmation would be invisible. Under distinct names the two sit side by side and the disagreement is on screen, which is the whole point of seeding wrong values. | A row is IN THE QUEUE while both target columns are blank. cell_count is a count aggregation ('count' is the only aggregation the v1 loader supports).",
    "business_key": "dt_job",
    "column_types": {
      "dt_job": "string",
      "dt_lot_confirmed": "string",
      "dt_slot_confirmed": "string",
      "cell_count": "number"
    },
    "display_columns": [
      "dt_job",
      "dt_lot_confirmed",
      "dt_slot_confirmed",
      "cell_count"
    ]
  },
  "eqp_frame_attribution": {
    "__comment": "[TRACE FIXTURE -- enrichment DERIVED table] One row per (equipment, product); the worklist for inference #2 (which of the 8 frames were these coordinates recorded in). The frame is fixed per equipment and product in principle, but the declaration never reaches us, so a human confirms it (user 2026-08-01). | TWO target fields, not one: core_frame and dt_frame are INDEPENDENT unknowns. Collapsing them into a single 'frame' column would encode the exact misreading corrected in the spec -- knowing the pair narrows 64 candidates to 8, it does not pick one. | Frame values are spelled 'rot<0|90|180|270>_<front|back>'. A genuinely undeterminable case must come back UNRESOLVED, not confidently wrong: the symmetric subsets in truth_ambiguous.csv are scored correct only when the answer is 'unknown'.",
    "business_key": "frame_key",
    "composite_key_source": ["dt_eqp", "product"],
    "composite_key_separator": "|",
    "column_types": {
      "frame_key": "string",
      "dt_eqp": "string",
      "product": "string",
      "core_frame": "string",
      "dt_frame": "string",
      "cell_count": "number"
    },
    "display_columns": [
      "frame_key",
      "dt_eqp",
      "product",
      "core_frame",
      "dt_frame",
      "cell_count"
    ]
  },
